# PROPOSED brain-db scope for the TUESDAY seat (Datasec). NOT live: braindb.sh
# reads only scope/<seat>.scope. Tuesday's coordinator reviews this file and
# copies it to scope/tuesday.scope to adopt it (see INSTRUCTIONS-for-other-seats.md).
# Exercised on fixtures only by tests/run.sh; never run against a real tree.

seat tuesday
own_clients datasec general

allow rules        CLAUDE.md
allow rules        0_Brain/CLAUDE.md
allow lesson       0_Brain/learnings/20*.md
allow rules_index  0_Brain/learnings/_rules_index.tsv
allow ledger       0_Brain/learnings/_ledger_laptop_datasec.md
allow ledger       0_Brain/learnings/_ledger_laptop_datasec_archive.md
allow daily        0_Brain/daily_tuesday/20*.md
allow skill        0_Brain/skills/*.md
allow identity     0_Brain/identity/*.md
allow people       0_Brain/people/*.md
allow architecture 1_Project_Definition/Architecture/*.md

deny_path (conflict_on_
deny_path .pre-

# Kept from round 3 as a second guard on folder names only. It is NOT what decides: since round 4 the closed
# table in braindb_index.py does (one folder per kind and exact ledger names, per seat), and a lesson is
# never left out for a seat's word in its file name.
deny_seat_word friday
deny_seat_word wednesday
